  "title": "# Build: UI Review plugin (Angel profile, Opus, one session, no sub-agents) The axHub tool is allow…",
  "asked": "# Build: UI Review plugin (Angel profile, Opus, one session, no sub-agents) The axHub tool is allowed in this launch: load CLAUDE.md, _claude/shared/rules/RULES.md, _claude/rules/RULES.md and _claude/THREADS.md through axhub.memory_read (project amberx-axf / shared, area claude) if claude-sync can't, then build. Branch claude/ui-review (this worktree, from main). Brett, Oct 30 2026 (voice, driving): rename the Design packs console plugin and make it one all-in-one UI approval plugin. Every UI a build makes goes there for his approval, separated by type, with design packs as one section. 1. Rename the design-packs plugin to **UI Review** (folder ui-review), following plugin-lifecycle@1: new folder + install/uninstall scripts, migrate its data (the 18 packs, rounds, 12 shots each, his picks) into the new dataDir, remove the old folder and every reference (menus, search, docs markers), keep View -> Design packs working as a shortcut into the Design packs section. MAX_PICKS 3 and the Pick flow stay. 2. Sections by kind (open registry, new kinds without code changes): Design packs, Whole apps / programs, Screens & pages, Settings interfaces, Dialogs & popups, Menus & toolbars, Banners & cards, Other. Each item: title, kind, app, build/branch/PR, screenshots (desktop + phone), notes, status (waiting / approved / changes asked / rejected), his comment, history. 3. Views, switchable and remembered: collapsible tree (kind > app > item, multi-select with checkboxes), collapsible grid with expandable panes (row expands to the shots + details), grid with sub-grids (group rows by kind or app, each group a sub-grid), gallery of large shots, side-by-side compare. Multi-select works in every view: bulk Approve / Ask changes / Reject. Filters, search, sort, counts per section, waiting-first. 4. How builds submit: a small CLI (node <plugin>/review.mjs submit --kind settings --title ... --shots a.png,b.png --branch ... --pr ...), the plugin API, and framework/cli/rebuild-shots.mjs gets an option to submit its shots. Expose capability ui-review@1 (pending/approved state per branch/PR) for other plugins. Do NOT edit the push-banner plugin (another build is changing it): add a THREADS note + an orchestrator follow-up step so the batch merge later holds PRs whose UI review is waiting or rejected. Add a rule line to _claude/shared/rules/RULES.md: every build that adds or changes UI submits its screenshots to UI Review. 5. Theme tokens only, framework controls, page head per DESIGN-LANGUAGE, phone-first (he works from a Galaxy S26 Ultra). Tests: test.py + test.mts for the data, the views' pure parts and the CLI; run console tsc + vite build, check-theme, check-controls, check-plugin-pages, plugin-lifecycle check for ui-review, menu-reach. Screenshots of every view with rebuild-shots.mjs. 6. Bookkeeping: add the build to the Angel orchestrator (_claude/builds/profiles/angel/orchestrator.json, split into steps of 30 min or less), THREADS.md row, change-log entry on axHub. Push the branch and open its PR through the push banner. Don't merge. Anything that needs Brett goes out as a veto call with a reason; never poll it.",
